1.bug_scenario:
When formatting Angular template code with pipes that take string or numeric arguments, Prettier 2.8.0 (parser "angular") inserts unwanted spaces around the colon separators. For example:

Input template:
```html
{{ (user$ | async).credit | currency:'CAD':'symbol-narrow':'4.2-2' }}
{{ (user$ | async).items | slice:1:5 }}
```

After running Prettier 2.8.0 (parser="angular"), the output becomes:
```html
{{ (user$ | async).credit | currency : 'CAD' : 'symbol-narrow' : '4.2-2' }}
{{ (user$ | async).items | slice : 1 : 5 }}
```

This diverges from the official Angular style (no spaces between pipe name and colon when arguments are literal strings/numbers) and from the user’s expected behavior.
